#: ../../../prop_tgt/SYCL_DEVICE_TARGETS.rst:2
msgid "SYCL_DEVICE_TARGETS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/SYCL_DEVICE_TARGETS.rst:7
msgid "Experimental. Gated by ``CMAKE_EXPERIMENTAL_SYCL``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/SYCL_DEVICE_TARGETS.rst:9
msgid ""
"List of device targets to generate code for.  Names are interpreted by the "
"SYCL compiler:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/SYCL_DEVICE_TARGETS.rst:12
msgid ""
"AdaptiveCpp accepts compilation flows with optional architecture lists, such "
"as ``generic``, ``omp.accelerated``, ``cuda.explicit-multipass:sm_80,"
"sm_86``, and ``hip.explicit-multipass:gfx90a``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/SYCL_DEVICE_TARGETS.rst:16
msgid ""
"IntelLLVM and DPClang accept SYCL target triples or architecture aliases, "
"such as ``spir64`` and ``intel_gpu_pvc``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/SYCL_DEVICE_TARGETS.rst:18
msgid ""
"Clang accepts offload target triples, such as ``spirv64-unknown-unknown``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/SYCL_DEVICE_TARGETS.rst:20
msgid ""
"The compiler installation must support the requested targets.  These values "
"are not interchangeable across compilers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/SYCL_DEVICE_TARGETS.rst:23
msgid ""
"This property is initialized by :variable:`CMAKE_SYCL_DEVICE_TARGETS` when a "
"target is created.  If unset or empty, the compiler's configure-time device "
"target selection is used.  A non-empty false value (for example ``OFF``) "
"suppresses CMake-generated device target options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/SYCL_DEVICE_TARGETS.rst:28
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/SYCL_DEVICE_TARGETS.rst:30
msgid ""
"if(CMAKE_SYCL_COMPILER_ID STREQUAL \"AdaptiveCpp\")\n"
"  set_property(TARGET app PROPERTY SYCL_DEVICE_TARGETS\n"
"    cuda.explicit-multipass:sm_80)\n"
"elseif(CMAKE_SYCL_COMPILER_ID MATCHES \"^(DPClang|IntelLLVM)$\")\n"
"  set_property(TARGET app PROPERTY SYCL_DEVICE_TARGETS intel_gpu_pvc)\n"
"endif()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/SYCL_DEVICE_TARGETS.rst:39
msgid ""
"Selections are applied to SYCL compilation and linking, including standalone "
"device linking when the host link uses another language. Set compatible "
"selections on targets that compile device code and on the target that links "
"it; this property is not a transitive usage requirement."
msgstr ""
